---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Reducing Tool Overload for Sourcing Associates - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Fortune 500 Retail</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Reducing Tool Overload for Sourcing Associates</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Fortune 500 mass-market retailer with multiple AI chat tools and sourcing systems across the enterprise</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Sourcing associates navigating multiple systems daily to complete basic tasks</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Associates had to visit too many different systems to get their job done; proliferating AI chat tools added noise without solving the underlying fragmentation</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">A product manager in the sourcing insights team at this Fortune 500 retailer described a tool sprawl problem that had grown worse, not better, with the rise of AI. The company had deployed multiple AI-powered chat tools across the organization — each branded, each with a different scope, each requiring associates to learn a new interface. As the PM bluntly put it: "So many freaking chat tools."</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The underlying problem was that associates still needed to visit too many different systems to complete basic sourcing tasks. Checking a supplier's history might require one tool. Pulling cost data required another. Finding the status of an RFQ meant checking a third. The AI chat tools were supposed to simplify this, but without transparency into how they reached their answers, associates defaulted back to Excel — the one tool that let them see the data and the logic at the same time.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Company leadership was actively clamping down on new point-solution tools. Any technology adopted by the sourcing organization needed to consolidate access, not add another tab.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker acts as a unifying layer across the associate's workflow. Rather than replacing each specialized system, it surfaces the relevant information from across tools within the context of the associate's current task. When an associate is reviewing a supplier communication, Marker pulls in the relevant cost history, RFQ status, and compliance documentation — without requiring the associate to open separate systems.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Critically, every piece of information Marker surfaces is traceable back to its source. Associates can see not just the answer but the communication or data record it came from. This transparency addresses the trust gap that caused teams to reject black-box AI tools. The result is fewer tabs, fewer logins, and fewer context switches — without requiring the organization to rip out and replace any existing system.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Single interface surfacing relevant data from across tools in the context of the associate's current task</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Full traceability from every surfaced insight back to its source record, building trust with skeptical users</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Consolidates access without replacing existing specialized systems — no rip-and-replace required</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Fewer context switches and system logins for associates completing daily sourcing tasks</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker reduces tool overload for your sourcing team.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
